---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Splitwise Limits & Alternatives — Roommate";
const description = "Splitwise now restricts free users to 3 expenses per day with 10-second wait timers. Here are the best free alternatives for flatmates in 2026.";
const keywords = "splitwise limits 2026, splitwise daily limit, splitwise review 2026, best free splitwise alternative, why splitwise has wait timer";

const articleSchema = {
  headline: title,
  description: description,
  datePublished: "2026-11-15T08:00:00Z",
  authorName: "Umesh Jaiswal"
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  keywords={keywords}
  ogType="article"
  publishDate="2026-11-15T08:00:00Z"
  articleSchema={articleSchema}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", url: "https://roommatesexpensemanager.com" },
    { name: "Blog", url: "https://roommatesexpensemanager.com/blog" },
    { name: "Splitwise 2026 Review", url: "https://roommatesexpensemanager.com/blog/splitwise-limits-and-best-free-alternatives-2026" }
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 space-y-8 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
    <header class="space-y-4 border-b border-slate-800 pb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-slate-500 font-medium">
        <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-rose-950 text-rose-400 border border-rose-800/40">App Comparisons</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>November 15, 2026</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>7 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Splitwise Limitations in 2026: Why You Need a Dedicated Free Alternative
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-400">
        From beloved student utility to frustrating paywalled product: an honest examination of the changes driving flatmates away from Splitwise.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white">The Enshittification of Splitwise</h2>
      <p>
        For nearly a decade, Splitwise was the default answer whenever roommates, travel buddies, or couples asked: <em>"How should we split bills?"</em>
      </p>
      <p>
        However, starting in late 2023 and intensifying throughout 2025 and 2026, Splitwise introduced severe restrictions on free users that disrupted basic day-to-day usability.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white">The 3 Major Friction Points</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-rose-950/20 border border-rose-900/40 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-rose-300 text-base">1. The 3 Expenses Per Day Restriction</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400">
            In an active flat with 3 roommates, you easily log morning coffee/milk, afternoon groceries, evening takeaway, and an electric bill on the same day. Capping entries at 3 turns a utility tool into a blocker.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-amber-950/20 border border-amber-900/40 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-300 text-base">2. The 10-Second Wait Screen</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400">
            To force free users to upgrade, the app forces an artificial 10-second countdown before you can tap "Save". When you are in a rush at a payment terminal, waiting 10 seconds is intolerable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-purple-950/20 border border-purple-900/40 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-purple-300 text-base">3. Pushy Pro Up-sells ($39.99/year)</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400">
            For college students and young professionals sharing a flat, spending ₹3,000+ per year just to log shared rent and tomatoes is completely impractical.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white">Why Roommate is Built Different</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Roommate</strong> was engineered to be what bill-splitting was always supposed to be: lightweight, fast, and completely free.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-slate-300 pl-2">
        <li><strong>No Limits:</strong> Log 50 expenses a day if you want.</li>
        <li><strong>No Ads or Timers:</strong> Saves instantly in milliseconds.</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile PIN Login:</strong> No passwords or SMS OTP friction.</li>
        <li><strong>Live Excel View:</strong> Real-time matrix view of the whole month.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer class="pt-8 border-t border-slate-800 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <p class="text-white font-bold">Switch to Roommate today.</p>
      <a href="/splitwise-alternative" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-500 text-white font-bold text-xs shadow-md transition">
        Compare Roommate vs Splitwise →
      </a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
